# Modern Web UI

- Use React/Next/Vite conventions already present in the project. Do not migrate frameworks unless explicitly asked.
- Inspect existing components, tokens, Tailwind setup, shadcn/Radix usage, icons, layouts, and copy style before adding UI.
- Build the usable product screen first. Avoid generic landing-page filler when the user asks for an app, dashboard, tool, CRM, panel, or workflow.
- Use semantic HTML, keyboard-accessible controls, visible focus states, labels, and correct loading/disabled/error states.
- Keep responsive layout intentional. Verify that text, buttons, cards, tables, dialogs, and navigation do not overlap on mobile or desktop.
- Prefer established UI primitives such as shadcn/ui, Radix UI, lucide-react, and the local design system when available.
- For Tailwind v4 projects, use the existing CSS-first theme approach. For older Tailwind projects, preserve their current config style.
- Use real assets or generated imagery for brand/product/place pages when visuals matter. Avoid generic gradients as the primary visual idea.
- Keep cards for actual repeated items, panels, modals, or tools. Do not nest decorative cards inside cards.
